# MCO Styles - Research Assistant Example
# This file defines styling preferences that are injected during formatting or presentation steps

@style Writing style
>Use a formal, academic writing style with proper citations and references.
>Write in clear, concise language that avoids jargon when possible.
>When technical terms are necessary, define them on first use.
>Use active voice rather than passive voice when appropriate.
>Maintain a neutral, objective tone throughout the report.

@style Formatting
>Use clear headings and subheadings to organize content.
>Include a table of contents for reports longer than 1000 words.
>Use bullet points for lists and numbered lists for sequential items or rankings.
>Keep paragraphs focused on a single idea, typically 3-5 sentences.
>Include page numbers and section references for longer documents.

@style Citations
>Use APA citation format for all references.
>Include in-text citations for all factual claims and quoted material.
>Provide a complete bibliography or references section at the end of the report.
>For web sources, include access dates and URLs.
>For academic papers, include DOI when available.

@style Visual elements
>Keep visual elements clean and minimal with a professional appearance.
>Use a consistent color scheme for all charts and graphs.
>Include clear titles and labels for all visual elements.
>Provide captions that explain the significance of each visual element.
>Ensure all visual elements are accessible and understandable in both color and black-and-white formats.